  "sections": {
    "work": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "La Galerie Notre-Dame (plate 9) is a very beautiful rendering of Gothic architecture, and a most delicate study of effects of light, direct and reflected. The impressions vary much, some being rich in tone and rather veiled, others clean wiped and of a silvery clearness.",
        "source": {
          "author": "Campbell Dodgson",
          "title": "The Etchings of Charles Meryon",
          "publisher": "The Studio (Internet Archive scan)",
          "year": "1921",
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/etchingsofcharle00dodguoft",
          "readAt": "https://archive.org/stream/etchingsofcharle00dodguoft/etchingsofcharle00dodguoft_djvu.txt",
          "tier": 2,
          "accessed": "2026-11-26",
          "page": "13"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "That gallery of Notre Dame, with Wotan's ravens flying through the slim pillars from a dream city bathed in sinister light, is not the only striking conception of the poet-etcher.",
        "source": {
          "author": "James Huneker",
          "title": "Promenades of an Impressionist",
          "publisher": "T. Werner Laurie (Internet Archive scan)",
          "year": "1910",
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/promenadesofimpr00huneuoft",
          "readAt": "https://archive.org/stream/promenadesofimpr00huneuoft/promenadesofimpr00huneuoft_djvu.txt",
          "tier": 3,
          "accessed": "2026-11-26",
          "page": "180"
        }
      }
    ],
    "moment": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "His Galerie Notre-Dame was refused by the Salon in 1853, and though many of his Paris etchings were exhibited there, they gained no prize.",
        "source": {
          "author": "Campbell Dodgson",
          "title": "The Etchings of Charles Meryon",
          "publisher": "The Studio (Internet Archive scan)",
          "year": "1921",
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/etchingsofcharle00dodguoft",
          "readAt": "https://archive.org/stream/etchingsofcharle00dodguoft/etchingsofcharle00dodguoft_djvu.txt",
          "tier": 2,
          "accessed": "2026-11-26",
          "page": "2"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "These etchings are magnificent things. We must not allow this splendid imagination to be worsted in the struggle. Strengthen him by all the encouragements possible.",
        "lead": "Victor Hugo, during Meryon’s lifetime:",
        "source": {
          "author": "Victor Hugo",
          "title": "Letter on Meryon’s etchings, quoted in Keppel, Charles Meryon: A Biographical Sketch",
          "publisher": "Frederick Keppel & Co. (Internet Archive scan)",
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/charlesmeryonbio00kepp",
          "readAt": "https://archive.org/stream/charlesmeryonbio00kepp/charlesmeryonbio00kepp_djvu.txt",
          "tier": 3,
          "accessed": "2026-11-26"
        }
      }
    ],
    "matters": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "He said that he had created an epoch in etching — which was the literal truth — and he had saved a rapidly vanishing Paris for the pious curiosity of future generations.",
